<title>ISRAEL: Israel Q1 new home sales decline.</title>
<headline>Israel Q1 new home sales decline.</headline>
<dateline>TEL AVIV 1997-07-08</dateline>
<text>
<p>Sales of private sector new homes in Israel in the first quarter of 1997 totalled 3,633, down 4.5 percent from the last quarter of 1996, the Central Bureau of Statistics said on Tuesday.</p>
<p>The figure is down 22 percent from the first quarter of last year.</p>
<p>The bureau said housing starts surpassed the number of homes sold, leading to an increase in inventory. It said 12,212 new homes were put up for sale in the first quarter against 11,917 in the previous quarter and 11,110 in the year earlier quarter.</p>
<p>-Tel Aviv newsroom, 972-3-537-2211 TCC</p>
